>   Why is the AK not complete at this point of the game?

Bad luck. 

In many games I have played, I have done the valley, gone up to my stash, 
alchemized and enchanted to 250HP and -35 AC, and said "Screw it," and gone
all the way down and all the way up. However, sometimes I don't have all
the tools I need and my options are:

 * try to ascend without them
 * look for items in Gehennom
 * pudding farm (or create monster farm or what have you)

My most recent game was an orc rogue who got a 0:1 Castle wand and didn't
have MR, reflection, magic marker, or hardly anything identified. She
had AC -9 and was having a tough time. So after doing the Valley, I
went back upstairs and used up my wand. I didn't wish for reflectio,
which was probably a mistake.  I did wish for:


 * 2 blessed scrolls of charging (got 1)
 * GDSM +3
 * magic marker
 * HoB +3
 * spellbook of identify

You can argue about the correctness of this wish set, but my other
options were to painstakingly ID things, wish for a magic marker and
burn a lot of identify scrolls, or just not bother with alchemy and
scroll identification  --- and rogues can get to skilled in divination,
which contains magic mapping, The Only Way To Fly In Gehennom. IDing
everything left me with some major holes:

 * no scrolls of gold detection
 * no glass orb (alternate means of gold detection)
 * no wands of death
 * no wands of cold
 * no wands of create monster
 * no scrolls of enchant armor

...and I think there were a couple of other things. Oh, no jumping boots,
but I had speed boots, so I could live. I polypiled all of my charges
and still came up dry on both gold detection and crystal ball; also,
no reflection.  I considered just going anyway, as I had done the planes
without portal detection at least once (I, uh, forgot my scrolls. *shame*)
, but then I accidentally hit my coaligned priest and was down to AC
-11 and that was the end of that plan.

